<<<
It is a relief to learn that limb does mean edge without a metaphor; the l. in Astronomy &c. is from Latin limbus hem, & the l. of ordinary speech is a separate & native word. See TRUE & FALSE ETYMOLOGY.
===
It is a relief to learn that *limb* does mean edge without a metaphor; the *l.* in Astronomy &c. is from Latin *limbus* hem, & the *l.* of ordinary speech is a separate & native word. See ^^TRUE^^ & ^^FALSE^^ ^^ETYMOLOGY^^.
>>>

<<<
limber, v., makes -ered &c.; see -R-, -RR-.
===
**limber, v.,** makes *-ered* &c.; see ^^-R-^^, ^^-RR-^^.
>>>

<<<
limbo. Pl. -os; see -o0(£)s 3.
