Sometimes used as a singular *(there is a good links here)*; cf. *an ironworks.*

**Linnaean, -nean.**
>>>

<<<
The first is usual, ‘ though the Linnean Society adopts the other form’ (OED). See Æ, a. Against -nean is the invariable spelling of Linnaeus.
===
The first is usual, ‘ though the Linnean Society adopts the other form’ (OED). See Æ, Œ. Against *-nean* is the invariable spelling of *Linnaeus*.
>>>

