<<<
lira, Italian franc, has pl. lire (pronounce Jéer’a) or anglicized liras. To use lira as pl. (A meal in a secondclass restaurant costs from eight to ten lira) is absurd.
===
**lira,** Italian franc, has pl. *lire* (pronounce le͞r'ă) or anglicized *liras.* To use *lira* as pl. *(A meal in a second-class restaurant costs from eight to ten lira)* is absurd.
>>>

