<<<
list, please. The third sing. pres. is list or listeth, the past tense list or listed. The verb being in any form archaic, it is of no great importance whether the more obviously archaic impersonal construction (as him list &c.) or the now commoner personal one (as he list &c.) is used.
===
**list, please.** The third sing. pres. is *list* or *listeth,* the past tense *list* or *listed.* The verb being in any form archaic, it is of no great importance whether the more obviously archaic impersonal construction *(as him list* &c.) or the now commoner personal one *(as he list* &c.) is used.
>>>

